y get  through it and then they just move on i  feel like that is the track it's going  to continue to stay on without any type  of dramatic change being forced because  it won't be forced without the threat of  litigation  and and we've expanded it mike and i'm  sure they'll expand it some way going  forward but unless owners are committed  to hiring a minority coach it's just not  going to happen at the same time i have  been as critical of anyone as houston  and and you have too we've been very  critical of the texans uh the past  however long months  but i will give them full credit for  this because just because no one's heard  of a head coach doesn't mean he can't be  a good head coach and we talk all the  time about minorities getting a chance  they're out there they just need to find  them houston did a great job of finding  one they think they can win with and  david calling and just because people  haven't heard about him doesn't mean  that he can't do a good job and he  hasn't done a good job in the past so  they hired a minority coach i will give  them full credit for that and i think  they had three minorities on their  finalist list for the head coaching  position so if i'm going to give houston  credit for anything it's going to be for  that but let me ask you this mike do you  think there would be less criticism if  eric the enemy had gotten say the  houston job instead of david cauley  would there have been less criticism now  of the league and it's minority hiring  i think if he'd gotten any job there  would have been less criticism because  let's face it with cully there's still  this perception and possible reality  that it was a jackie used to be inside  job that this is a guy that jackie used  to be knows won't threaten the fiefdom  that he used to be has created he's  going to be so grateful to have a job at  age 65 when it looked like his ship was  never going to come in the ship wasn't  even on the horizon for david cully so  all of a sudden